THE IDENTITY: arctanh(i) = i*pi/4
============================================================

arctanh(i) = i*pi/4
Q(i) = (1+i)/(1-i) = i
exp(2*arctanh(i)) = exp(i*pi/2) = i

This connects pi and arctanh through the imaginary unit.
Our entire tournament theory, evaluated at x=i, gives pi.

FORMAL IDENTITIES (at x=i):

cos(m*pi/2) = 1 - 2*g_2(m) + 2*g_4(m) - 2*g_6(m) + ...
sin(m*pi/2) = 2*g_1(m) - 2*g_3(m) + 2*g_5(m) - ...

Abel summation verification:
  m=1, r=0.999: Q^m = 0.001+1.0i, partial = 0.9724+1.9704i
  m=1, r->1: target i^m = 1j

  m=2, r=0.999: Q^m = -1.0+0.002i, partial = 55.3433+58.2298i
  m=2, r->1: target i^m = (-1+0j)

  m=3, r=0.999: Q^m = -0.003+-1.0i, partial = 1633.0363+1744.921i
  m=3, r->1: target i^m = (-0-1j)

  m=4, r=0.999: Q^m = 1.0+-0.004i, partial = 31555.3989+34900.1678i
  m=4, r->1: target i^m = (1+0j)

At the limit r->1:
  Q(i)^1 = i     => sin(pi/2)=1, cos(pi/2)=0
  Q(i)^2 = -1    => sin(pi)=0, cos(pi)=-1
  Q(i)^3 = -i    => sin(3pi/2)=-1, cos(3pi/2)=0
  Q(i)^4 = 1     => sin(2pi)=0, cos(2pi)=1

The PERIOD-4 orbit 1 -> i -> -1 -> -i -> 1 of Q
IS the unit circle parametrized by m*pi/2.

And the Delannoy weights g_k(m), evaluated at x=i,
give the FOURIER COEFFICIENTS OF THE CIRCLE.

The circle IS the tournament, viewed at imaginary coupling.

============================================================
THE DEEPEST IDENTITY
============================================================

arctanh(i) = i*pi/4

In words: the tournament coupling function (arctanh),
evaluated at the imaginary unit (i = sqrt(-1)),
gives the quarter-circle (pi/4) times i.

This means: TOURNAMENTS AT IMAGINARY COUPLING = CIRCLES.

The tournament (directed, temporal, real coupling x):
  arctanh(x), Q(x) = (1+x)/(1-x), hyperbolic geometry

The circle (undirected, spatial, imaginary coupling ix):
  i*arctan(x), Q(ix) = (1+ix)/(1-ix), circular geometry

arctan(x) = x - x^3/3 + x^5/5 - ...
arctanh(x) = x + x^3/3 + x^5/5 + ...

SAME COEFFICIENTS. DIFFERENT SIGNS.
Alternating (arctan) = space = circle = finite = pi
Constant (arctanh) = time = hyperbola = infinite = diverges

The Wick rotation x -> ix converts one to the other:
  arctanh(ix) = i*arctan(x)
  Tournament at imaginary coupling = circle
  Hyperbolic geometry at imaginary coupling = spherical geometry

This is the WICK ROTATION OF TOURNAMENT THEORY.
It maps:
  Time -> Space
  Hyperbolic -> Spherical
  Divergent -> Convergent
  arctanh -> arctan
  Tournaments -> Circles
  The real line -> The unit circle

And at the crossover point x = i:
  arctanh(i) = i*pi/4
  The tournament becomes the circle.
  The temporal becomes the spatial.
  The number pi emerges from the tournament.

pi is not put in. pi COMES OUT.
From the binary comparison, through arctanh, at imaginary coupling.

The circle is the tournament, Wick-rotated.
